+    # OHOS suspends on SIGSTOP but never reports the stopped state (see the
+    # note in tests/support/test.tcl). Two further cluster cases depend on
+    # fixed platform windows instead of on that stopped state:
+    #   * 12.1-replica-migration-3.tcl "Resharding all the master #0 slots
+    #     away from it" drives `valkey-cli --cluster rebalance`, whose
+    #     CLUSTER SETSLOT pre-replicates the command to every online replica
+    #     and blocks for at most CLUSTER_OPERATION_TIMEOUT (2000 ms) before
+    #     replying "-NOREPLICAS Not enough good replicas to write."; every
+    #     eligible replica has to ack inside that window.
+    #   * 28-cluster-shards.tcl "Kill a node and tell the replica to
+    #     immediately takeover" kills the primary and then immediately asks
+    #     the replica to take over; the reply it can hit ("ERR You should
+    #     send CLUSTER FAILOVER to a replica") is produced only while that
+    #     node already owns the primary flag, i.e. the case races the
+    #     platform's cluster failure-detection window - the same window that
+    #     already makes the next case of that file ("Verify health as fail
+    #     for killed node") platform-restricted.
+    # Fail closed: once a case of a file is skipped, the remaining cases of
+    # that file are skipped too, so no case can wait forever for a state a
+    # skipped case was meant to produce.
+    if {[info exists ::env(VALKEY_TEST_SKIP_PROCESS_PAUSE)]} {
